// case: generic-union-empty-construction-in-an-argument-prints-one-refusal
// what: `take(Option.None())` against an `int` parameter writes no type for the
//      union anywhere, so the construction is refused. It was refused four
//      times over two wordings: the callee's member was read as a value before
//      the Call arm decided the construction (`this expression`), and every
//      argument was checked a second time inside checkCallArgTypes, which ran
//      the whole node again (`the construction`). calleeIsTemplateConstruction
//      answers the construction question once now, and checkCallArgTypes reads
//      the types the call site already computed. `one-diagnostic:` pins the
//      count; `n124` pins the wording.
// expect-error: carries no payload, so nothing in the construction says which instantiation
// one-diagnostic:
union Option[T] {
    Some(T)
    None
}

fn takeNumber(n: int) -> int {
    return n
}

fn main() -> int {
    return takeNumber(Option.None())
}
